  "description": "Exploratory sugar for reading an unfamiliar sheet in a LINQPad script or a notebook: address a cell the way the file does (sheet.At(\"B4\")), and scaffold a first record declaration from a header row and a handful of sample rows. A separate package because nothing in the library uses any of it — a declaration that ships should be written against Unrect's own vocabulary, not this one.",
